## v1.1.2b1

Changes since v1.1.0 (beta):

+ Add `eos-usage` to measure managed EOS cache usage through a read-only REANA job.
  Report per-project live, non-live and unknown bytes, classification timestamps,
  incomplete scans and uniquely attributable legacy flat caches.
+ Add preview-first `eos-cleanup` and integrate REANA EOS cleanup into `tidyup`.
  Preserve live caches by default; unknown entries require `--include-unknown`.
  `--clear-project UUID` explicitly includes that project's live caches.
  Execution requires `--execute` and a confirmed manifest. Resume using plan IDs.
+ Validate recent scans, live sets, runner identity and metadata fingerprints;
  refuse active project workflows and changed manifests. Verify deletions using
  an independent read-only REANA job. Partial or uncertain runs are not retried
  automatically; unassigned caches are skipped.
+ Include `cache_on_runner` preferences from the full dependency graph when
  submitting a project or selected tasks.
+ Exclude `__pycache__`, `.pyc` and `.pyo` from impression tree comparisons,
  content hashing and file diffs, including historical trees. Generated bytecode
  no longer causes spurious source changes.
+ Set CelebiChrono to `1.1.2b1`; use matching Yuki for EOS operations.

The VS Code extension is versioned separately. Source preparation does not imply
publication of this beta to PyPI.
